<rml>
<head>
    <title>Letterbox</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <style>
        /* THE BARS OF A Z TARGET AND A CUTSCENE (2026-09-24; the user: "the black bar at top and
           bottom of screen animates in very very chappy rather than smooth when z targeting").
           The game makes them by scissoring the picture, and that scissor can only move once per
           game update; these are drawn over the picture instead and their height is set every
           frame the program presents, so they slide rather than step.

           No transition and no animation here on purpose: the easing is done in the program, in
           the game's own units and at the game's own speed, so the bars arrive exactly when the
           game believes they have. A transition on top would fight it. */
        body {
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            top: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            pointer-events: none;
        }
        .bar {
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 0px;
            background-color: #000000ff;
        }
        .bar.top { top: 0; }
        .bar.bottom { bottom: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="bar top" id="letterbox-top"></div>
    <div class="bar bottom" id="letterbox-bottom"></div>
</body>
</rml>
